# Which sections of the app this build ships. Entries are deltas against the
# defaults in src/features.ts (feed, events, connections and profile on; chat
# off), applied left to right:
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURES=chat            turn chat back on
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURES=-connections    hide the People tab
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURES=chat,-profile   both
#
# Known names: feed, events, connections, chat, profile. A disabled section
# loses its tab AND its routes, so a deep link into it lands on the home tab
# instead of a half-rendered screen. Unknown names are ignored with a warning
# in dev. Leave unset to ship the first-release set.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURES=

# Self-hosted Supabase stack (Kong -> GoTrue + PostgREST) behind api.aisocratic.org.
# These mirror NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY in the website repo.
# The anon key is a public, RLS-scoped JWT — safe to ship in a client bundle.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.aisocratic.org
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_KEY=

# Used for deep links back to the website (share sheets, "read on web").
EXPO_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://aisocratic.org

# Chat relay. Chat is a real Nostr client, and buzz.xyz (Block's open-source
# Slack alternative) is a Nostr deployment — there is no hosted Buzz API, SDK or
# npm package, its servers ARE Nostr relays. The app reads the relay's NIP-11
# document at startup and adapts:
#
#   Buzz community        NIP-29 groups (kind 9 + `h`), NIP-17 gift-wrapped DMs,
#                         NIP-42 AUTH required, members only.
#   public relay          NIP-28 rooms (kind 42 + `e`), NIP-04 DMs, open access.
#
# The default is the AI Socratic Buzz community. It is CLOSED: a key that is not
# a member cannot even complete AUTH (`restricted: not a relay member`), so each
# user redeems an invite code in the app's Chat tab. Codes are minted by the
# community owner via `POST /api/invites` and are NEVER embedded here — an
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ value ships inside the JS bundle, and Buzz invites can be
# unlimited-use, so committing one would make a private community public.
#
# For a public-relay deployment (no invite needed) use:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_NOSTR_RELAY=wss://relay.primal.net
# Verified public alternatives: wss://nostr.oxtr.dev, wss://nostr-pub.wellorder.net
# Beware: nos.lol, offchain.pub and nostr.land refuse writes from keys outside
# their web of trust, which every new user of this app has.
EXPO_PUBLIC_NOSTR_RELAY=wss://aisocratic.communities.buzz.xyz

# Automatic community joining.
#
# Where the app asks for an invite on the signed-in user's behalf. It sends its
# Supabase session JWT; the server checks the account, mints a single-use invite
# that expires in five minutes, and returns it. The app redeems it immediately
# with its own key, so the user never sees or types a code.
#
# This is a URL, not a secret, and that is the whole design. The key that can
# mint invites belongs to a community owner/admin and stays on that server as
# BUZZ_OWNER_KEY (website repo, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix). It must never appear
# here: every EXPO_PUBLIC_ value is plain text inside the JS bundle, and an
# extracted owner key mints unlimited invites to a private community.
#
# Leave it unset and nothing breaks — the app falls back to asking for a pasted
# invite code, which is how joining worked before this existed.
EXPO_PUBLIC_BUZZ_JOIN_URL=https://aisocratic.org/api/buzz/join
